    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Is there a function $f(x)$, other than $f(x)=0$, where the graph of $y=f'(x)$ is identical to the original?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. $f(x)=e^x$, since $f'(x)=e^x$.",
      "worked": "Take $f(x)=e^x$. Then $f'(x)=e^x=f(x)$, so the two graphs are identical.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
